{
    "test_name": "MOB.860_MaterialLookup_Cycle_Count",
    "details": {
        "name": "MOB.860_MaterialLookup_Cycle_Count",
        "type": "browser",
        "status": "paused",
        "message": "`MOB.860` Cycle count: adjust the fixture item's quantity and put it back.\n- **SELF-RESTORING BY ARITHMETIC**: `+1` then `-1` returns the item to its starting\n  quantity, so stock does not drift. Do not change this to only add.\n- Fixture `000-000-000 Adamantium` in `Central Storeroom`, reason `Error Correction`.\n- The modal closing is genuine proof: `close()` sits inside the mutation's `update()`\n  with no optimisticResponse, so it only fires on a confirmed server response. The\n  toast is transient and therefore optional.\n- This is the checklist's **Cycle count** item. `Material issue`/`Material return` are\n  NOT on this screen \u2014 they are work-order charges, covered by MOB.370.",
        "tags": [
            "Mobile",
            "env:dev",
            "Material Lookup",
            "CRUD"
        ],
        "locations": [
            "gcp:us-west2"
        ],
        "config": {
            "assertions": [],
            "config_variables": [
                {
                    "id": "fe7958bf-435f-4932-af8e-0931caab79e7",
                    "name": "MOBDEV",
                    "type": "global"
                }
            ],
            "request": {
                "headers": {},
                "method": "GET",
                "url": "{{ MOBDEV }}"
            },
            "variables": [
                {
                    "id": "fe7958bf-435f-4932-af8e-0931caab79e7",
                    "name": "MOBDEV",
                    "type": "global"
                }
            ],
